{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BvLScELb5gbGQR1PPgZVoX","type":"tool_result","content":"180\t    `gemini-2.5-pro` or `grok-4`, in the environment or in a settings\n181\t    `env` block. An agent file with such a `model:` passes\n182\t    `validate-governance.sh`.\n183\t  - The shipped `availableModels` is unchanged.\n184\t- **The Codex pin moved from an exact payload hash to a version floor.**\n185\t  - Before, `check_pair_rail.py --verify-codex-pin` failed closed on any\n186\t    Codex binary whose payload sha256 differed from the signed manifest,\n187\t    which pins one binary of Codex CLI 0.160.0.\n188\t  - Now a Codex CLI newer than the manifest version passes as\n189\t    `compatible/version_floor_only` when a nearby `@openai/codex`\n190\t    `package.json` declares a stable version at or above 0.160.0\n191\t    (`_lib/cli_currency.py`). The payload's sha256 is still computed and\n192\t    recorded, but on this route a mismatch with the manifest no longer\n193\t    fails.\n194\t  - The release gate follows: `validate-pair-rail-verdict.py` only checks\n195\t    the format of the payload sha of a verdict that declares such a\n196\t    version. Its range check reads the pin file; its payload-hash\n197\t    exemption uses the code constant 0.160.0\n198\t    (`cli_currency.CODEX_VERSION_FLOOR`).\n199\t  - The ADR-182 amendment states the floor as `>=0.160.0`. The pin file\n200\t    reads `>=0.128.0`, with no upper bound: a CI fix in the same pull\n201\t    request lowered it after the amendment.\n202\t  - The operating contract still says the reviewer is pinned by hash, not\n203\t    by range. That no longer describes `main`.\n204\t  - Installs do not receive `.claude/governance/`, so there the pin still\n205\t    resolves as infrastructure and fails open (advisory). That is\n206\t    unchanged.\n207\t  - With `--harness codex`, the installer now prints that it was verified\n208\t    against Codex CLI 0.160.0, while the hook fixtures date from 0.139.0.\n209\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33c378c0-c6a8-475a-b029-4896d83549f9","uuid":"10d24e3d-00b8-4832-85c1-f6ce6487bbd1","timestamp":"2026-11-16T17:52:19.736Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/CHANGELOG.md","content":"    `gemini-2.5-pro` or `grok-4`, in the environment or in a settings\n    `env` block. An agent file with such a `model:` passes\n    `validate-governance.sh`.\n  - The shipped `availableModels` is unchanged.\n- **The Codex pin moved from an exact payload hash to a version floor.**\n  - Before, `check_pair_rail.py --verify-codex-pin` failed closed on any\n    Codex binary whose payload sha256 differed from the signed manifest,\n    which pins one binary of Codex CLI 0.160.0.\n  - Now a Codex CLI newer than the manifest version passes as\n    `compatible/version_floor_only` when a nearby `@openai/codex`\n    `package.json` declares a stable version at or above 0.160.0\n    (`_lib/cli_currency.py`). The payload's sha256 is still computed and\n    recorded, but on this route a mismatch with the manifest no longer\n    fails.\n  - The release gate follows: `validate-pair-rail-verdict.py` only checks\n    the format of the payload sha of a verdict that declares such a\n    version. Its range check reads the pin file; its payload-hash\n    exemption uses the code constant 0.160.0\n    (`cli_currency.CODEX_VERSION_FLOOR`).\n  - The ADR-182 amendment states the floor as `>=0.160.0`. The pin file\n    reads `>=0.128.0`, with no upper bound: a CI fix in the same pull\n    request lowered it after the amendment.\n  - The operating contract still says the reviewer is pinned by hash, not\n    by range. That no longer describes `main`.\n  - Installs do not receive `.claude/governance/`, so there the pin still\n    resolves as infrastructure and fails open (advisory). That is\n    unchanged.\n  - With `--harness codex`