{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch72sr9KWbU7cfMmcWeXw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found no P0, and none of the declared conditions is false against this payload, so the decision is GO. Six P2 follow-ups and no new P1 findings.\n\n**What I checked against the candidate tree:**\n- **Condition 5 holds.** The kernel list includes the new audit-emit package (`check_arbitration_kernel.py:312`) and all 13 declared rows (lines 309-315, 332-336 and 340).\n- **Condition 7 holds.** `audit_emit.py` is now a thin entry point that hands its 33 parts to `install()` (lines 413-452).\n- **The moved audit-emit code still behaves the same.**\n  - `install()` rebinds each moved function onto the entry point's namespace, so name lookups, `global` writes and test patch points still go through `_lib.audit_emit`.\n  - Mutable values are deep-copied on each import.\n  - No part redefines `emit_generic`, `_KNOWN_ACTIONS`, `EVENT_SCHEMA_V2` or `emit_credential_rotation_due`.\n  - I traced every outside name this payload's parts use, and each one resolves.\n  - Only three other modules import the package, and they use only `install()`.\n- **`ceo-boot.md`'s \"25 Tier-S checks\" is true:** there are 25 entries, with an assert (`scheduled_cache.py:303-370`).\n- **The unbounded Codex pin range parses everywhere.** The release-gate validator accepts a missing upper bound (`validate-pair-rail-verdict.py:345-359, 609-624`), and so does the installer script (`scripts/_codex_harness.sh:76-86`).\n- **Condition 10 holds.** \"Compatible\" needs version 0.160.0 or higher *and* newer than the manifest (`cli_currency.py:11, :34-51`; `part_01.py:557-567`). The CHANGELOG (lines 184-208) describes the change honestly.\n- **Fail direction and writes are safe.** The context-pressure marker and shard-cursor writes stay fail-open. They use symlink-refusing temp files plus atomic replace, and cleanup is limited to the marker prefix.\n- **Version files agree on 1.4.4** (`npm/package.json`, `plugin.json`, `marketplace.json`). The code is standard library only and compatible with Python 3.9.\n\n**P2 follow-ups:**\n1. **Dead second action registry in kernel code.** `actions.py:12`, `actions_core.py:4` and `actions_extended.py:4` are never installed; the live registry is the literal at `audit_emit.py:45-377`. Their docstrings cite a `schemas_actions` module that doesn't exist. A maintainer could register an action there and it would silently stay unregistered. Fix: delete the three files, or add a test that the two registries are equal.\n2. **Pin-file comment misstates \"compatible\".** `codex-cli-pin.txt:196-198` says versions from 0.128.0 up are compatible evidence; the oracle actually requires 0.160.0 and newer than the manifest. Lines 165-166 still call widening only the upper bound \"the only safe shape\", which this change no longer follows. Already disclosed in CHANGELOG 199-201 and condition 9. Fix: reword the comment.\n3. **`install()` only rebinds plain functions** (`__init__.py:21-48`). A future part exporting a class or wrapped callable would keep its own globals and bypass patches. None does today. Fix: raise `TypeError` on any other exported callable.\n4. **`ceo-boot.md:43-50` is incomplete.** It says 25 checks across 6 categories but lists only 15 names (pre-existing gap). Fix: list all 25, or drop the category list.\n5. **Stale \"four rails\" wording.** `defense.py:18-25` and the comment at `actions_extended.py:302-306` say four rails, but the rail enum now also has `bash_indirect` (`lifecycle_schemas.py:508`). Doc only.\n6. **Latent validator gap (cross-reference; the code belongs to another payload).** `validate-pair-rail-verdict.py:770-773` skips the payload-hash check for any version at or above 0.160.0 that differs from the manifest version, including versions *older* than the manifest. The oracle and CHANGELOG:188 require newer. It can't trigger today because the manifest is at 0.160.0, the same as the floor. It would after a re-pin above the floor. Fix: also require the version to be newer than the manifest before skipping the hash check.\n\n**Limits:** I couldn't check the new hashes in `gate-scripts-manifest.txt` (redacted copy, no shell); only CI reads it, so a mismatch would fail CI loudly. I couldn't diff the moved code line by line against the base, so equivalence was checked by structure. I couldn't confirm from the tree that only the conditions file changed between the rc and GA."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1083,"cache_read_input_tokens":201132,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1083},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33c378c0-c6a8-475a-b029-4896d83549f9","uuid":"961e6aaf-10b5-439f-867e-9ee37a56d46b","timestamp":"2026-11-16T17:52:51.734Z","request_id":"req_011Ch72squBX8iDZFQd85pax"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch72sr9KWbU7cfMmcWeXw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015YzKzVUKroCtvt8PsBRzwP","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"report":"PAYLOAD 1/34 (v1.4.3-rc.1..84b83324c820): what it contains\nVersion bumps (.claude-plugin/marketplace.json, .claude-plugin/plugin.json, .claude/.framework-version -> 1.4.4); .claude/commands/ceo-boot.md 24 -> 25 Tier-S checks; .claude/governance/codex-cli-pin.txt \">=0.128.0,<0.161.0\" -> unbounded \">=0.128.0\"; gate-scripts-manifest.txt new hashes for validate-governance.sh, release.sh and validate-pair-rail-verdict.py; the new package .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/ (__init__.install, actions*, adapters, boot_schemas, compaction, confidence, context_pressure, defense, federation_persona, federation_schemas).\n\nVERIFIED AGAINST THE CANDIDATE TREE\n- Condition 5: .claude/hooks/check_arbitration_kernel.py:312 carries \".claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/**/*\"; the other declared rows are at :309-315, :332-336 and :340. The new package in this payload is kernel-covered.\n- Condition 7: .claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py is a thin entry point. It calls _install_parts(globals(), 33 part names) at :413-452.\n- Moved code (item 4):\n  - install() (__init__.py:21-48) rebinds every exported FunctionType onto the facade's globals. Lookups of _write_event, emit_generic, _breadcrumb and _scrub_ceo_boot_event, global writes (writer._FALLBACK_NOTIFIED) and test patch points therefore all go through _lib.audit_emit.\n  - Mutable declarations are deep-copied once per import, with one shared memo, so aliases such as _MCP_CANONICAL_GUARD_BLOCKED_ALLOWLIST stay intact. Compiled regexes deepcopy to themselves.\n  - No part exports emit_generic, _KNOWN_ACTIONS, EVENT_SCHEMA_V2 or emit_credential_rotation_due. Only replay exports iter_events, and the re-delegation at audit_emit.py:455-461 behaves as its comment says.\n  - I traced every outside name used by this payload's parts: the defense.py enums and allowlists (harness_schemas.py:10 and lifecycle_schemas.py:9 __all__), the writer helpers (writer.py:5-33), _PERSONA_MATCH_MODALITY_ENUM (boot_schemas), the _CONTEXT_PRESSURE_* constants (compaction), and zlib/os/time/Path/re (audit_emit.py:2-12). Every one resolves.\n  - _lib.redact.redact_secrets exists (redact.py:120).\n  - Outside the facade, only lessons.py:204 and check_agent_spawn.py:128 import the package, and they use only install().\n- ceo-boot.md \"25 Tier-S checks\" is true: TIER_S_CHECKS has 25 entries, with an assert (.claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/scheduled_cache.py:303-370). The CHANGELOG (:340, :479) documents main_checkout_state.\n- The unbounded pin range parses in every consumer I checked:\n  - validate-pair-rail-verdict.py:345-359 and :609-624 accept an optional upper bound.\n  - scripts/_codex_harness.sh:76-86 skips a missing max.\n  - pair-rail-gate.sh gates on the payload-pin oracle.\n  Condition 9 and CHANGELOG [1.4.4] :184-208 declare the change honestly.\n- Condition 10: \"compatible\" requires >= CODEX_VERSION_FLOOR 0.160.0 and a version strictly newer than the manifest (cli_currency.py:11, :34-51; _pair_rail_parts/part_01.py:557-567). The manifest package_version is 0.160.0.\n- Item 2 (fail direction) and item 3 (writes): context-pressure hysteresis and GC stay fail-open on I/O errors. The marker and shard-cursor writes use O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW random-named temp files plus os.replace. GC unlinks only names with the marker prefix and removes symlinks rather than their targets (context_pressure.py:73-290).\n- Item 6: everything is standard library only. The code is Python 3.9 compatible: FunctionType(code, globals, name, defaults, closure); annotations as strings under the future import; frozenset|set unions; no runtime PEP 604/match syntax.\n- Version sites agree: npm/package.json, .claude-plugin/plugin.json and marketplace.json are all 1.4.4.\n\nP0: none.\nDECLARED CONDITIONS FOUND FALSE IN THIS PAYLOAD: none.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex): none at P1.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\n1. P2 - .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/actions.py:12, actions_core.py:4, actions_extended.py:4. A dead duplicate action registry sits in kernel code.\n   - \"actions\" is not in the install roster (audit_emit.py:415-451). The live registry is the literal at audit_emit.py:45-377.\n   - Both docstrings say \"combined by schemas_actions\", and no module of that name exists.\n   - Failure scenario: a maintainer registers a new action only in actions_extended.py. It stays unregistered at runtime and is dropped to a breadcrumb.\n   - Fix: delete the three files, or add a test asserting actions._KNOWN_ACTIONS == audit_emit._KNOWN_ACTIONS, and correct the docstrings.\n2. P2 (honesty, already disclosed) - .claude/governance/codex-cli-pin.txt:196-198. The comment says releases \">= 0.128.0 are compatible version evidence\".\n   - The oracle's \"compatible\" actually requires >= 0.160.0 and a version newer than the manifest.\n   - Lines :165-166 still call widen-upper-only \"the only safe shape\".\n   - Effect: scripts/_codex_harness.sh no longer prints VERSION SKEW for any Codex 0.161 or later, while the hook fixtures are still certified on 0.139.0.\n   - Declared in CHANGELOG [1.4.4] :199-201, :207-208 and condition 9.\n   - Fix: reword the comment to say the range is the installer and validator version gate only, and that \"compatible\" requires CODEX_VERSION_FLOOR and a version newer than the manifest.\n3. P2 - .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/__init__.py:37-48. install() silently skips any exported callable that is not a FunctionType.\n   - A class, functools-wrapped callable or partial would keep its template module's globals. It would then bypass facade patches, or raise NameError on facade-only names.\n   - No current part (audit_emit, agent_spawn, lessons) exports one.\n   - Fix: raise TypeError on such exports.\n4. P2 (doc) - .claude/commands/ceo-boot.md:43-50. The text says \"25 Tier-S checks across 6 categories\" but lists only 15 check names. The gap predates this delta, and the count bump widens it to 10. Fix: list all 25, or drop the category enumeration.\n5. P2 (doc, trivial) - .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/defense.py:18-25 and actions_extended.py:302-306 say learning_rail_disabled is shared by \"four\" rails. _LEARNING_RAIL_ENUM (lifecycle_schemas.py:508) now also carries \"bash_indirect\", emitted by bash_indirect_telemetry.py:59-65. Fix: update the wording.\n6. P2 (latent; cross-reference, the code is in another payload) - .github/scripts/validate-pair-rail-verdict.py:770-773.\n   - exact_payload_pin is False whenever codex_cli >= CODEX_VERSION_FLOOR and differs from the manifest version, including when it is OLDER than the manifest.\n   - cli_currency.compatible_package_version and CHANGELOG :188 require strictly newer.\n   - It is vacuous today, because the manifest (0.160.0) equals the floor. After a re-pin above the floor without raising CODEX_VERSION_FLOOR, a verdict declaring an older version would pass with an unattested payload sha.\n   - Fix: exact_payload_pin = version_comparison is None or version_comparison <= 0 or newer_floor is None or newer_floor < 0.\n\nLIMITS OF THIS REVIEW\n- I did not hash the files named in gate-scripts-manifest.txt: the tree is redacted and I had no shell. Only CI workflows read that manifest, so a mismatch fails CI loudly; it does not reach adopters.\n- I had no base tree, so moved-code equivalence was checked by structure (name resolution, binding mechanics, duplicate exports, registry), not line by line.\n- I could not confirm from this tree that only CONDITIONS-ga.md changed between the rc tag and the GA candidate.","decision":"GO","sentence":"Payload 1 has no P0 and leaves every declared condition true against the candidate tree: the kernel list covers the new audit_emit package, the split binds and resolves every name through the facade with its fail-open and